### Maintenance — Homebase API
### Base URL: http://localhost:3000
###
### Photos are uploaded as multipart/form-data under the field name "photos"
### (repeat the field for multiple files). A ticket accepts up to 5 images of
### 8 MB each. Tenants may omit unitId/tenantId — both are derived from their
### active tenancy. Owners filing on a tenant's behalf must send both.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@unitId = 0192f58e-4a61-7bf0-8e6f-47dc2e0f49f3
@tenantId = 0192f58e-4a61-7bf0-8e6f-47dc2e0f49f1
@propertyId = 0192f58e-4a61-7bf0-8e6f-47dc2e0f49f5
@ticketId = REPLACE_WITH_TICKET_ID

### 1. Report a fault as a tenant (unit + tenant derived server-side)
POST {{baseUrl}}/maintenance
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----homebase

------homebase
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="description"

Kitchen tap is leaking continuously.
------homebase
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="photos"; filename="tap.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./photos/tap.jpg
------homebase--

### 2. File on a tenant's behalf as the owner (unitId + tenantId required)
POST {{baseUrl}}/maintenance
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----homebase

------homebase
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="description"

Bathroom door lock broken.
------homebase
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="unitId"

{{unitId}}
------homebase
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="tenantId"

{{tenantId}}
------homebase
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="photos"; filename="door.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./photos/door.jpg
------homebase--

### 3. Report a fault with no photos at all
POST {{baseUrl}}/maintenance
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

description=Bulb in the corridor is out
&unitId={{unitId}}
&tenantId={{tenantId}}

### 4. List tickets (scoped to the caller's role automatically)
GET {{baseUrl}}/maintenance

### 5. List only open tickets
GET {{baseUrl}}/maintenance?status=OPEN

### 6. List tickets for one property
GET {{baseUrl}}/maintenance?propertyId={{propertyId}}

### 7. Paginated
GET {{baseUrl}}/maintenance?page=1&limit=20

### 8. Single ticket (photoUrls are returned as absolute URLs)
GET {{baseUrl}}/maintenance/{{ticketId}}

### 9. Move a ticket into progress
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/maintenance/{{ticketId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "IN_PROGRESS"
}

### 10. Resolve a ticket (stamps resolvedAt)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/maintenance/{{ticketId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "RESOLVED"
}

### 11. Reopen a resolved ticket (clears resolvedAt)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/maintenance/{{ticketId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "OPEN"
}

### 12. Edit the description only
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/maintenance/{{ticketId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "Tap replaced, checking the sink trap for a slow leak."
}

### 13. Delete a ticket (also deletes its objects from R2)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/maintenance/{{ticketId}}
